.el .ds Aq '
.TH acc-manpage 1  "manpage 0.5.4" 
.SH NAME
acc\-manpage \- Generate man pages
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBacc manpage\fR [\fB\-\-out\-dir\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate man pages
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-out\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Write one page per command into DIR instead of printing acc.1 to stdout
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress status lines on stderr
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Write acc.1 (the top\-level page) to FILE instead of stdout
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print extra diagnostics on stderr (resolved policy, format, destination, counts). Never changes stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Never color diagnostics. acc\*(Aqs own output is never colored; this and a non\-empty NO_COLOR environment variable switch off color in help and usage errors too
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH VERSION
v0.5.4
